        "original_id": "1ae8503f-4951-5468-8461-f82715c4b6b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: WS-15, Chengdu J-20\n- Organizations: Shenyang Aeroengine Research Institute, Xi'an Aero-Engine Corporation, Chengdu Aerospace Corporation, People's Liberation Army Air Force\n- Concepts: afterburning turbofan engine, supercruise, stealth, twinjet, fifth-generation fighter aircraft\n\nFacts:\n- The Chengdu J-20 is a stealth, twinjet, fifth-generation fighter aircraft developed by China's Chengdu Aerospace Corporation for the People's Liberation Army Air Force.\n- The WS-15, codenamed Emei, is a Chinese afterburning turbofan engine designed by the Shenyang Aeroengine Research Institute and manufactured by the Xi'an Aero-Engine Corporation.\n- The WS-15 is used to power China's Chengdu J-20 fighter.\n- The WS-15 would enable the Chengdu J-20 to achieve supercruise.",
